From: Fathom <fathom@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: ingenic: usb: don't disable the VCC regulator in exit

The VCC supply is enabled in .power_on and disabled in .power_off. .exit
disabled it a second time, so the usual phy_power_off() + phy_exit()
sequence (dwc2 does this in probe for peripheral-only ports) triggers
"unbalanced disables for regulator-dummy". Leave the regulator to the
power callbacks; .exit only stops the clock that .init started.

Signed-off-by: Fathom
---
diff -Naur a/drivers/phy/ingenic/phy-ingenic-usb.c b/drivers/phy/ingenic/phy-ingenic-usb.c
--- a/drivers/phy/ingenic/phy-ingenic-usb.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/ingenic/phy-ingenic-usb.c
@@ -124,7 +124,6 @@
 	struct ingenic_usb_phy *priv = phy_get_drvdata(phy);
 
 	clk_disable_unprepare(priv->clk);
-	regulator_disable(priv->vcc_supply);
 
 	return 0;
 }
